CORE
memory_x_bit_writes.sv
--top main --bound 3
^\[main\.p_low\] .*: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.p_high\] .*: PROVED up to bound 3$
^\[main\.p_keep\] .*: PROVED up to bound 3$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
A Yosys-style byte-masked memory write: 32 guarded bit writes at a runtime
address, with x for the bits outside the enabled byte. The x is inside the
array update, which the commit does not sample, so the merged value is bound
to auxiliary wires (unbound, this took more than 5 GiB).
